Programming language name: Aether

	This lab included the design of two statements to be implemented into the language. 
I included making two new Java classes to create objects of the two types of statements (Print and expression statements). I also made sure to update the error handling to check for missing semicolons, plus the synchronization function. 
	I updated the parser class to return a list of statements, and when I use the parser in the main file, it starts with a grammar rule of "statement" that checks if the list of tokens represents a print or expression statement. I also included an update to the error handling in the parser by adding a synchronize function that checks whether the next token is either "print" or ";" to know if the parser is safe to continue parsing. The function to help synchronize the panic mode will be updatable as we continue adding more features to the language as well. 
	I was also able to update how the evaluator part of the language works by making it able to interpret a list of statements that the parser returns. For every statement in the list that is passed to the evaluator, it evaluates the statement, and if it is a print statement, it prints it to the terminal, it just consumes the statement and does not print anything to the terminal. 
	The only change to my main Aether file was changing the logic to line up with the new parser/evaluator files. I made sure to create a list for the parser return statement to go to and then gave that list to the evaluator. 

For the test cases provided, I was able to input the test cases and successfully get outputs for them. My language gave me a single error for the missing ';' after the first line. The language also took the statements on lines 3 and 4 and combined them into one statement. It took the print statement on line 3 and continued it through the next line. So instead of reporting an error that "print 2 +" was missing a semicolon, it stated that the printed statement was evaluated to 8 (2+4+2 = 8). The rest of the statements printed out perfectly normal as they should. 
